<?xml version="1.0" standalone="yes"?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name "npm-auto">
<!ENTITY author "dTrolley">
<!ENTITY github "&author;/&name;">
<!ENTITY launch "Settings/npm-auto">
<!ENTITY plugdir "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/&github;/main/&name;.plg">
<!ENTITY version "2026.10.01">
<!ENTITY md5 "ec1ddc6979ed34573cad78e142e76013">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" launch="&launch;" pluginURL="&pluginURL;" icon="random" support="https://www.github.com/dTrolley/npm-auto" min="7.0.0">
    <CHANGES>
### 2026.10.01
- Settings page rebuilt the Unraid way: Apply/Done, inline help, Yes/No
  choices, a status line, and settings kept in npm-auto.cfg (written by
  Unraid's update.php). Existing settings are converted on upgrade; the old
  var/settings.json is kept as settings.json.migrated
- Enabling or disabling now starts or stops the service; Apply restarts it so
  changes take effect at once. Disabling leaves NPM untouched
- NPM host may be left blank to mean this server
- The saved NPM password is never sent to the browser; blank keeps it
- Disable all / Delete all work with the service off; new View log button
- Fix: the Auto Proxy switch borrowed the Docker page's "autostart" class,
  which broke the Basic/Advanced view switch. It now uses Unraid's own
  switch widget, found by column position (works in translated webGUIs)
- Docker tab warns on the Auto Proxy header when the service is off or
  cannot reach NPM
- Daemon: one docker inspect per pass instead of several per container,
  and only switched-on or managed containers are examined; stops promptly
- getState also reports service, running, health and version (unraid-mobile)
- Switch and subdomain changes are locked against each other and validated
  against existing containers; changes require POST
- Login JSON built with jq and passed on stdin; non-hostname domains refused
- Build fixed for Linux/CI; same-day versions zero-padded

### 2026.09.28-1
- New Subdomain column on the Docker tab, after Auto Proxy: shows the name
  each proxied container is served at, and a click sets an override (kept in
  state.json, so no container recreate). A live entry is renamed on the next
  pass, and its certificate re-picked for the new name
- Fix: NPM answers an expired token with HTTP 400, not 401, so the daemon
  kept reusing it and stopped reconciling. It now logs in again
- Identical log lines are written at most once an hour, and the log is
  trimmed past 5 MB: /var/log is a 128 MB tmpfs shared with syslog
- The Subdomain column also shows hand-made NPM entries (muted), matched to
  their container by name, forward host or published port
- Docker tab only refetches state when rows are added, not on every live
  CPU/memory update; script and stylesheet are cache-busted on upgrade

### 2026.07.18-3
- Stamp-based auto-adoption: entries bearing the npm_auto meta stamp are
  re-adopted on domain OR target match (heals container renames and plugin
  reinstalls); adopted entries are stamped too
- Fix: include locations[] in created entries and normalize it on updates
  (NPM rejected updates to daemon-created entries with a 400 otherwise)
- Skip no-op state.json writes to spare the flash device

### 2026.07.18
- Settings pre-fill for fresh installs: NPM host defaults to the Unraid
  host's detected LAN IP, port defaults to 81 (both customizable)
- Enforce forward host on managed entries: a host LAN IP change now
  bulk-updates every managed proxy host automatically (re-detected each
  reconcile cycle, no daemon restart needed)

### 2026.07.17-9
- Strict adoption: existing entries are adopted only when domain AND forward
  target both match; conflicts reject the toggle with a specific error
- Adopted hosts are fully managed thereafter (same policies as created ones)
- New "Auto-attach matching SSL certificate" setting
- Label override syntax (npm-auto.domain / npm-auto.port) documented on the
  settings page

### 2026.07.17-7
- Auto-select an unexpired NPM certificate (exact or wildcard match) for new
  proxy hosts; force SSL when one is found
- Reconcile drift: created hosts follow default-domain/port/cert changes
- Adopt pre-existing hosts matching a container's domain without rewriting them
- New "toggle-off action" setting: Keep / Disable / Delete
- Cleanup controls on the settings page + prompt when disabling the plugin
- Uninstall never touches NPM entries

### 2026.07.17-2
- Fix settings persistence (PHP variable-scope bug) and CSRF token handling
- Unify settings as JSON shared by the settings page and daemon
- Remove debug logging that leaked session cookies to a public share
- Restore GitHub URL-based .plg install flow (was pointing at wrong branch)
- Implement NPM proxy-host reconciliation daemon (create/adopt/delete hosts)
- Add array started/stopping event hooks to manage the daemon
- Strip macOS metadata from packages

### 2025.11.07
- Initial Release by Gemini
    </CHANGES>

    <FILE Name="/boot/config/plugins/&name;/&name;-&version;.txz" Run="upgradepkg --install-new">
        <URL>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/&github;/main/archive/&name;-&version;.txz</URL>
        <MD5>&md5;</MD5>
    </FILE>

    <FILE Run="/bin/bash">
        <INLINE>
            # Remove old package archives, keep the current one
            find /boot/config/plugins/&name;/ -name "&name;-*.txz" ! -name "&name;-&version;.txz" -delete
            mkdir -p /boot/config/plugins/&name;/var
            echo "&version;" > /boot/config/plugins/&name;/version
            &plugdir;/scripts/migrate-settings.sh
            # Start, restart or stop the daemon to match the settings, so an
            # upgrade runs the new code at once
            &plugdir;/scripts/rc.npm-auto apply
            echo ""
            echo "----------------------------------------------------"
            echo " &name; has been installed."
            echo " Version: &version;"
            echo "----------------------------------------------------"
            echo ""
        </INLINE>
    </FILE>

    <FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
        <INLINE>
            &plugdir;/scripts/rc.npm-auto stop
            removepkg &name;-&version;
            rm -rf &plugdir;
            rm -rf /boot/config/plugins/&name;
        </INLINE>
    </FILE>
</PLUGIN>
